{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1432929983,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU4MjU2NjU5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/156","origin":"github"},"title":"Debian git-annex-based data packages","message":"This is primarily to keep the notes about the issues for whenever we start automagically compose debian packages for those\n1. dpkg-deb spends quite a bit of time even on simple ones (e.g. pymvpa2-tutorialdata) probably due to excessive number of symlinks if in indirect mode\n2. but in direct mode we might still be left with some symlinks (http://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/symlinks_to_absent_files_remain_upon_switching_to_direct_mode).\n3. for packages with some data pre-fetched/contained (if we decide to do so) it might be worth building inplace only source packages, but then for binary packages outof the tree so that git-annex doesn't get pollutted with all the gets/drops (upon clean)\n4. git-buildpackage doesn't support 3.0 (git) source format (yet)\n5. \"ultimate\" purge of the installed annex might need 'rm' of the entire directory in postrm script happen people pulled in some additional files","files":null}]}